/* book Worked example 2: Q: An S-band search radar at 3 GHz has a 4 m dish with efficiency 0.55, peak power 1 MW, pulse width 1 µs and PRF 1000 Hz. Find the beamwidth, the gain in dB and the average power.
   1. λ = 3 × 10⁸ / 3 × 10⁹ = 0.1 m.
   2. Beamwidth: θ ≈ 70λ/D = 70 × 0.1 / 4 = 1.75°.
   3. Gain: G = η(πD/λ)² = 0.55 × (π × 4 / 0.1)² = 0.55 × 125.66² = 0.55 × 15 791 = 8685, and 10 log10 8685 = 39.4 dB.
   4. Duty cycle: 10⁻⁶ × 1000 = 0.001; Pav = 10⁶ × 0.001 = 1 kW.
   Answer: θ ≈ 1.75°, G ≈ 8685 (39.4 dB) and Pav = 1 kW: the waveguide carries 1 MW pulses while the cooling handles only 1 kW. */
